<title>LEBANON: Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 702 bln pounds.</title>
<headline>Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 702 bln pounds.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's weekly treasury bill issue of October 17 raised 702 billion Lebanese pounds, the finance ministry said on Monday.</p>
<p>The previous issue raised 741 billion pounds.</p>
<p>The new issue posted a nominal surplus of subscription against maturity of 134 billion pounds. It raised the following amounts (in billions of pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term			  Yield		    Amount</p>
<p>    Three months	    14.61 (14.61)	   106.9 (91.8)</p>
<p>    Six months		16.92 (16.92)	   185.2 (219.8)</p>
<p>    12 months		 17.78 (17.79)	   131.4 (134.7)</p>
<p>    24 months		 21.62 (21.64)	   278.4 (294.6)</p>
<p>The Lebanese pound closed at 1,557 to the U.S. dollar on Monday from 1,557.50 a week earlier and 1,607 a year ago.</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 602057 645456</p>
